      en: "The Lifoula River, a 150-kilometer-long tributary of the Louessé, flows through the Lefini Wildlife Reserve in southern Congo. The reserve, established in 1951, protects 440,000 hectares of savanna and gallery forest. The river supports a population of African manatees (estimated 120 individuals) and over 200 bird species. The Lifoula's average width is 30 meters, with a depth of 2–4 meters. Annual fish catch from the river is around 50 tons, primarily tilapia and catfish. The river is culturally significant to the Téké people, who consider certain stretches sacred. Ecotourism initiatives include canoe trips and birdwatching.",
      es: "El río Lifoula es un curso de agua tranquilo en el departamento de Pool que serpentea a través de densos bosques de galería y tierras agrícolas fértiles. Desemboca en el río Congo y sirve a las comunidades locales como principal fuente de agua potable y pesca. Las zonas ribereñas son ricas en plantas silvestres utilizadas tradicionalmente con fines medicinales.",
