      en: "Lake Lakou, located in the Pool Department, is a volcanic maar lake formed by a phreatomagmatic eruption approximately 10,000 years ago. It has a diameter of 1.5 km and a maximum depth of 85 meters. The lake's water is acidic (pH 5.5) and oligotrophic, limiting aquatic life to a few adapted species. Two endemic cichlid fish species are found here. The lake is surrounded by dense tropical forest and is part of a protected area established in 2005. For the local Lari people, the lake is a sacred site used for ritual offerings. A small ecotourism project started in 2016, offering guided hikes and boat tours.",
