      en: "The Sese River, 170 km long, flows through the Likouala region in northwestern Congo. Its basin of 2,800 km² is covered with pristine rainforest. The river has an average discharge of 80 m³/s, dropping to 20 m³/s in the dry season. It is about 20 m wide and 1–3 m deep. Fisheries yield around 50 tons annually, mainly Nile perch and tigerfish. A proposal to establish a national park in the area was submitted in 2010 but has not been finalized. The river is home to Baka Pygmy communities who use traditional fishing methods. Wildlife includes gorillas, chimpanzees, and forest elephants.",
